				"_note": "Statutory-deadline archetype: a filing's whole purpose is 'was it filed on time and is proof retained', so the page leads with the deadline/submittedDate/paidDate/electronicallyFiled facts in the data widget, no stat KPIs (the fields are dates/booleans, not summable amounts) and no related panel (the schema carries no employeeId/administrationId or any other object-FK -- a filing is an organisation-level record, not scoped to a person). Files is included full-width for the filed submission/deposit proof, justified by the schema's own retainedUntil/furnishedToRecipientDate/filedWithAuthorityDate retention-evidence fields (NL 7yr / DE 6yr / US 4yr retention obligations). No calendar/comms leaves -- deadline is a plain date field, not an appointment/event linkedType. No lifecycleActions -- the schema declares no `status` field or x-openregister-lifecycle; submittedDate/paidDate are plain timestamps, not a guarded state machine. Audit history is a sidebar tab.",
